# Motion and 3D

- Use Client Components for GSAP, refs, browser APIs, `@react-three/fiber`, and `@react-three/drei`.
- Scope GSAP animations with `gsap.context(..., ref)` and clean them up with `ctx.revert()`.
- Prefer `useLayoutEffect` for layout-sensitive GSAP work and `useEffect` for non-layout animation setup.
- Register GSAP plugins once per module before use, for example `gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger)`.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences for large movement, long timelines, parallax, or 3D scenes. Use `usePrefersReducedMotion` when adding new animated sections.
- Mark purely decorative motion or shapes with `aria-hidden` and keep the meaningful content available as text.
- Avoid animating layout-heavy properties when transform or opacity can achieve the same effect.

```tsx
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  const ctx = gsap.context(() => {
    gsap.from(elementRef.current, { autoAlpha: 0, y: 24 });
  }, containerRef);

  return () => ctx.revert();
}, []);
```
